Welcome to TUS - Toasty Unix Software.

This machine boots a kernel of its own: a higher-half x86-64 kernel with
a round-robin scheduler, a virtual filesystem, a TCP/IP stack, a window
system in the kernel (highX) and a shell (tsh) the terminal windows are
views onto.

Some places to start:

  help                 the shell's built-in commands
  highx --de           the desktop (log in at the greeter)
  highx --wm           the tiling window manager instead
  tusinstall           install this system onto a disk
  clint                the browser
  kilo /etc/motd       the editor

Accounts live in /etc/passwd and /etc/shadow; `useradd` makes one and
`passwd` gives it a password. Until it has one, the greeter lets that
account in with an empty password and says so.

Sound, a writable on-disk filesystem and symmetric multiprocessing are
not here yet. Everything else in this mail is.

